# A fast flight across a cube edge and past a cube corner, with the
# coverage tree checked every frame: no overlapping draws, no visible drawn
# chunk without a mesh, nothing left uncovered.
#
# Faces: 0 is +X, 2 is +Y, 4 is +Z (cubesphere FACES). The +X/+Y edge is the
# meridian lon 45; the (+X, +Y, +Z) corner is lat 35.26, lon 45.
#
#   leg 1: lat 0, lon 30 -> east at 1 km/s for 30 s (30 km): crosses lon 45
#          after ~24 km, onto face 2.
#   leg 2: lat 20, lon 44.5 -> north at 1 km/s for 50 s: passes ~800 m from
#          the corner and onto face 4 (+Z).

mode fly
speed 1000
at 0 30 3000
look 90 0
assert face == 0
assert mode == fly
travel 30
assert face == 2
assert travel_violations == 0
assert travel_overlaps_max == 0
assert travel_gaps_max == 0
assert travel_uncovered_max == 0
assert travel_frames == 1800
shot 01_after_edge

at 20 44.5 3000
look 0 0
assert face == 0
travel 50
assert face == 4
assert lat > 48
assert travel_violations == 0
assert travel_overlaps_max == 0
assert travel_gaps_max == 0
assert travel_uncovered_max == 0
shot 02_after_corner

# And low and fast over the ground near the edge, where the horizon hides
# most of the tree: 250 m up at 400 m/s, back across lon 45.
at 0 46 250
look 270 0
speed 400
travel 20
assert face == 0
assert travel_violations == 0
shot 03_low_back_across_edge
bench 60
